body:
## Summary

Reduces the first-prompt context further after GH#32444, with no loss of guidance, skills, or invocation paths. The four items from #32592 ship together:

1. **On-demand dispatcher for rare OC1 plugin tools.** `gpt_image_generate`, `model-accounts-pool` and `aidevops_objective_receipt` move behind one `aidevops_on_demand` tool. Its description lists a one-line signature per sub-tool. If `args` is omitted, the dispatcher returns the full sub-tool JSON schema without executing. Invalid args return the validation issues plus the schema, so the model can self-correct.
2. **Stable plugin greeting on OC1.** OC1 now uses the same root-session gate as OC2, so the greeting block is identical on every request of an interactive root session. The block carries the resolved aidevops and OpenCode versions. The generated runtime-config AGENTS.md fallback is wrapped in markers, and the plugin removes it from the prompt while its greeting is enabled. Headless and child sessions get neither the block nor the fallback.
3. **Legacy home and Git-root AGENTS.md templates retired.** Setup no longer deploys them. A new migration moves only byte-identical historical copies, matched by git blob hash against all 31 historical template versions, to `~/.aidevops/config-backups/migrations/gh32592-agents-md/`. Edited copies stay in place, as does a home copy that a legacy AI CLI memory file still references.
4. **Pointer-sized `agent__intent` schema.** The injected per-tool description is now `See Intent Tracing.`: 71 chars per tool instead of 171. The full instruction is still in the system prompt.

## Measured results

The method isolates the PR's effect:

- one Haiku first request per run;
- the same isolated XDG config each time, with only the aidevops plugin swapped;
- control is the deployed v3.37.6 plugin; candidate is this branch;
- control and candidate run back to back from the same checkout;
- tokens are API-reported (`input + cache_read + cache_write`).

| Runtime / case | Control chars | Candidate chars | Δ chars | API tokens |
|---|---:|---:|---:|---|
| OC1 1.18.32, interactive root | 89,335 | 84,062 | −5,273 (−5.9%) | 24,049 → 22,698 (−1,351, −5.6%) |
| OC1 1.18.32, headless worker | 89,329 | 82,482 | −6,847 (−7.7%) | 24,046 → 22,358 (−1,688, −7.0%) |
| OC2 2.0.3 | 76,708 | 75,369 | −1,339 (−1.7%) | — |

- **OC1 tools:** 38,440 → 33,739 chars (22 → 20 tools). The dispatcher replaces 4,164 chars with 1,363, and the intent pointer saves 100 chars per tool.
- **OC1 runtime AGENTS.md section:** 2,513 → 393 chars. Interactive roots gain the resolved greeting block (+~1.5K chars). That removes the turn-1 `VERSION` and greeting-cache reads the fallback required.
- **In the aidevops repo only:** the trimmed project `.opencode/tool` descriptions (`ai-research`, `session-rename`, `session-rename_sync_branch`) save another 452 chars.
- **OC2:** intent −1,200 (12 tools) and the compact greeting block −137. The legacy Git-root AGENTS.md (3,048 chars in the OC2 capture) is removed by the migration on deploy, which takes OC2 to about −4.4K chars.
- **Estimate correction:** #32592 expected roughly 4–5K fewer OC1 tokens. Its token figures were char-based estimates. The API-reported saving is 1.35–1.7K Haiku tokens per first request, and it repeats in the cached prefix of every later request.

## Constraints verified live

- **OAuth wire shape unchanged:**
  - `system` stays `[billing header with cch, Claude Code identity]`;
  - framework text is redistributed into `messages[0]`;
  - every non-builtin tool keeps the `mcp__aidevops__` prefix;
  - `agent__intent` is present on 20/20 OC1 tools and 12/12 OC2 tools.
- **Prompt-cache prefix stable across turns:** in a two-request OC1 session, `system`, `tools` and the `messages[0]` text are byte-identical; only the trailing `cache_control` breakpoint moves. Turn 2 reports `cache_read` 22,734, which equals the full turn-1 prefix (9,145 read + 13,589 write).
- **Dispatcher end to end:**
  - Anthropic OAuth (Haiku):
    - omitted args return the schema;
    - an invalid enum returns issues plus the schema;
    - a valid `model-accounts-pool` status call executes.
  - OpenAI OAuth (`gpt-5.6-terra`): a valid call executes.
  - Both providers accept the open `args` object schema.
- **Per-agent gating kept:** `aidevops_mcp` stays direct.

## Deviations from the brief

- **Item 1 scope:** three of the seven listed tools moved.
  - Kept direct: `aidevops_mcp` (per-agent gating) and `aidevops` (frequent CLI entry).
  - `ai-research` and `session-rename*` are project-local `.opencode/tool` tools, so their descriptions were trimmed instead of wrapped.
  - OC2 is unchanged, because Code Mode already defers plugin tools.
- **Item 2 approach:** instead of slimming the fallback, it is delimited and stripped while the plugin greeting is enabled. The complete fallback remains on disk for sessions where the plugin is disabled (`AIDEVOPS_PLUGIN_SESSION_GREETING=0`) or fails to load. The pinned precedence phrases stay in the plugin block.
- **Item 3 extra:** removed the orphaned `templates/home/git/.agent/README.md`, which has no deploy or doc reference.
- **`setup.sh`:** the interactive silent migrations moved into `_setup_run_interactive_silent_migrations`, so `_setup_run_interactive` stays under the 100-line function gate.

## Changes

- **Item 1:**
  - `.agents/plugins/opencode-aidevops/on-demand-tools.mjs` (new);
  - `index.mjs` (OC1 wiring only);
  - `subagent-effort-escalation.mjs` (the receipt reminder names the dispatcher);
  - `tools.mjs` (JSDoc);
  - `.opencode/tool/ai-research.ts` and `.opencode/tool/session-rename.ts` (descriptions).
- **Item 2:**
  - `greeting.mjs` (default on, fallback markers, `stripGreetingFallback`);
  - `ttsr.mjs` (compact block, strip);
  - `root-session-greeting-gate.mjs` (memoised root lookup, `openCodeV1SessionLookup`);
  - `oauth-pool-token-endpoint.mjs` (detected OpenCode version);
  - `index.mjs`;
  - `.agents/scripts/generate-runtime-config-agents.sh` (markers).
- **Item 3:**
  - `.agents/scripts/setup/modules/migrations.sh` (`cleanup_legacy_agents_md_templates`);
  - `setup.sh`;
  - `templates/deploy-templates.sh` (workspace README only);
  - `templates/home/AGENTS.md`, `templates/home/git/AGENTS.md` and `templates/home/git/.agent/README.md` removed.
- **Item 4:** `provider-auth-body.mjs` (`INTENT_PARAM_SCHEMA`).
- **Tests:**
  - new `tests/test-on-demand-tools.mjs` and `.agents/scripts/tests/test-legacy-agents-md-migration.sh`;
  - updated greeting-gate, TTSR, token-advisory, subagent-effort and greeting-precedence tests.
- **Docs:**
  - `.agents/reference/context-efficiency.md`;
  - `.agents/reference/agent-routing.md`;
  - `.agents/tools/build-mcp/aidevops-plugin.md`;
  - `.agents/tools/vision/image-generation.md`;
  - `.agents/workflows/models-pool-check.md`.

## Verification

- **Plugin suite in the worktree** (no `node_modules`): 998 tests, 991 pass, 5 skipped (Zod-dependent). The 2 failures are environmental:
  - `test-opencode-v2-adapter.mjs` needs `@opencode/plugin`. It passes 16/16 in a mirror with the deployed dependencies and an isolated HOME.
  - `test-bounded-interactive-operation.mjs` passes 12/12 in isolation. It is timing-sensitive under full-suite load, and this PR doesn't touch it.
- **Plugin tests in the mirror (Zod available):**
  - `test-on-demand-tools.mjs` 8/8;
  - `test-tool-args-schema`, `test-gpt-image-tool`, `test-oauth-pool-display`, `test-subagent-effort`, `test-token-advisory-threshold` (17/17), `test-ttsr-system-transform` and `test-session-start-greeting-gate` all pass.
- **Project tools:**
  - `bun build` of both `.opencode/tool` files;
  - `bun test .opencode/lib/ai-research.test.ts` (16 pass);
  - `.agents/scripts/tests/bun/test-session-rename-ts.mjs` passes.
- **Shell:**
  - `test-legacy-agents-md-migration.sh` passes under macOS `/bin/bash` 3.2 and bash 5, including `IFS=$'\n\t'`;
  - `test-greeting-precedence.sh` passes;
  - `test-legacy-dashboard-launchagent-cleanup.sh` 2/2;
  - `test-managed-temp-workspace.sh` 19/19;
  - ShellCheck is clean;
  - `linters-local.sh --changed` exits 0.
- **Blob list:** every historical blob of both templates (following renames) matches the 31 listed hashes exactly.
- **Not run:** `tests/test-batch-quality-hardening.sh` fails before reaching this PR's code. It references `supervisor-helper.sh`, removed in #2291, and CI doesn't run it. Tracked as a follow-up.

## Post-merge checks

After the release and `aidevops update`:

- the OC1 runtime-config AGENTS.md contains the `aidevops:greeting-fallback` markers;
- setup moved the unmodified legacy Git-root AGENTS.md into the migration backup directory, and a fresh OC2 capture no longer loads it;
- fresh OC1 and OC2 captures match the candidate numbers above;
- an interactive OC1 session greets once with resolved versions.

## Follow-ups

These will be filed separately:

- trim the built-in Bash/Task/TodoWrite descriptions via `tool.definition`;
- deduplicate the framework AGENTS.md against the Build+ prompt;
- OC2 capture gaps;
- the empty observability `runtime_version`;
- `AIDEVOPS_HEADLESS=1` for the non-interactive `opencode run` harnesses;
- the stale batch-quality test.

Resolves #32592
